--- body ---
`tests/test_new.sh` has individual tests for magic line, log separator, body separator,
Title, Author, and Created headers (lines 39–79). These are all subsumed by the
"generated file passes erg validate" test at line 33: if `erg validate` passes, all format
invariants are satisfied by definition.

The individual checks add line count and maintenance burden without adding diagnostic value
— a failure in "log separator present" means exactly the same thing as a failure in
"generated file passes erg validate".

Action: remove the 6 redundant field-check tests (lines 39–79) and add a comment above
the `erg validate` test at line 33 explaining it subsumes all structural checks:

  # Subsumes: magic line, log/body separators, Title/Author/Created headers.
  # If validate passes, all format invariants are satisfied.

Leave the `erg validate` test itself unchanged.
